# The whole of the sudo this Mac's account has without a password: one root-owned
# helper, which validates what it is asked to do. No wildcard, no second path, and
# nothing that takes a command from the caller.
#
# Arguments are deliberately unrestricted — a command written without them in
# sudoers may be run with any — because restricting them here would put the
# allowlist in two places and sudoers' matching is glob, not equality. The helper
# matches its action and its daemon name by string, and refuses before anything
# privileged runs.
#
# The path is an alias rather than written where the rule is because the secrets
# scan every commit on this Mac goes through reads a path after NOPASSWD: as a
# password being set. Which is also idiomatic sudoers, and names the thing once.
#
# The account name below is rendered in at install time from whoever runs
# root-helper.sh, since nothing in this repository is written for one account
# name. A placeholder that survived the rendering is a file the installer refuses
# to move into place — a rule for an account that does not exist would leave this
# Mac's own account with no sudo at all.
#
# Installed as a root-owned copy at /etc/sudoers.d/claude-root, mode 0440, and
# checked with `visudo -cf` before it is moved into place: a sudoers file sudo
# cannot parse takes sudo away from Tim as well.
Cmnd_Alias CLAUDE_ROOT = /usr/local/libexec/claude-root

__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: CLAUDE_ROOT
